# supercronic schedule for the Zeabur worker.
#
# Times are Asia/Taipei (the container sets TZ), NOT UTC. The GitHub Actions
# workflows express the same schedule in UTC because GH runners are UTC-only;
# writing them in Taipei time here removes the standing conversion bug where
# someone "fixes" 08:30 UTC thinking it is the Taipei morning slot.
#
# These run IN PARALLEL with the GitHub Actions workflows, by explicit choice.
# Safe because every writer upserts on composite primary keys, so a double run
# is a no-op rather than a duplicate. The one thing that is NOT idempotent is
# the Telegram message layer — which is why TELEGRAM_TOKEN is intentionally
# unset on this service. Setting it makes every alert arrive twice.

# ── Post-close pipeline — 16:30 Taipei, weekdays ────────────────────────────
# Market closes 13:30; the buffer is for TWSE/MOPS to publish closing data.
30 16 * * 1-5 /app/deploy/daily-chain.sh

# ── Margin catch-up — 21:00 Taipei, weekdays ────────────────────────────────
# The MI_MARGN fetcher is NOT broken; TWSE simply publishes 融資融券 after the
# 16:30 harvest window. Measured 2026-07-31 at 18:36 Taipei: the endpoint
# returned stat='OK' with 1,060 rows for 07-30 and
# 「很抱歉,沒有符合條件的資料」 for 07-31. So the post-close run can only ever
# record an empty day, which left M1's subitem 3 (margin) permanently
# data_missing and unscored.
#
# a1bafbd already made an `empty` logged on a real trading day retryable
# instead of a permanent skip — but nothing ran later to take the retry. This
# is that run. Idempotent: upsert on (date, ticker_id).
0 21 * * 1-5 python -m src.backfill.run --days 3 --only margin

# ── Risk Guard pre-market restatement — 08:30 Taipei, weekdays ──────────────
# The 試撮 window, before the 09:00 open. Has to land before the operator can
# place an order — that is the only moment a restatement is worth anything.
30 8 * * 1-5 python -m riskguard.pipeline --mode pre_market

# ── News harvest — REMOVED 2026-07-31, deliberately ─────────────────────────
# Six `python -m src.news.harvest` slots used to live here (07:30 / 10:00 /
# 12:00 / 14:30 / 21:00 / 06:00 Taipei). The `newswatch` service now polls the
# same feeds every 180s, so these were re-fetching what a continuous poller had
# already ingested minutes earlier.
#
# Do NOT restore them because news looks stale — check `newswatch` first, and
# check `ingestion_log`, where the poller writes `source='news_watch'` rather
# than `'news_harvest'`. A third path would corrupt nothing (every writer
# upserts on the canonical-URL PK); it would just be work nobody reads.
#
# `.github/workflows/news_harvest.yml` still runs those six slots and stays as
# the backstop — it is the one path that survives this container being down.
# See docs/wiki/decisions/2026-07-31-near-realtime-news-poller.md.
